Right.

266
00:11:39,080 --> 00:11:40,080
They want to end the conversation.

267
00:11:40,080 --> 00:11:42,900
And, well, you want to end it in a polite way.

268
00:11:43,200 --> 00:11:44,200
Right.

269
00:11:44,200 --> 00:11:45,660
So they use a really great phrase here.

270
00:11:46,040 --> 00:11:49,520
They said, it's been great talking to you, but I have to get going.

271
00:11:49,840 --> 00:11:50,020
Right.

272
00:11:50,340 --> 00:11:54,340
So it's like, well, it's been great talking to you, but I have to get going.

273
00:11:55,400 --> 00:11:57,100
So it's been great talking to you.

274
00:11:57,900 --> 00:11:59,600
I've enjoyed talking to you.

275
00:11:59,820 --> 00:11:59,960
Right.

276
00:12:00,720 --> 00:12:06,320
So this is a very polite, very subtle way of saying, hey, I have to go or bye, I can't talk anymore.

277
00:12:06,500 --> 00:12:09,280
Yeah, when you say that, you know that the conversation is ending.

278
00:12:09,620 --> 00:12:09,920
Exactly.

279
00:12:10,620 --> 00:12:12,680
Now, she says, I have to get going.

280
00:12:12,860 --> 00:12:13,200
What does it mean?

281
00:12:13,920 --> 00:12:14,920
Get going.

282
00:12:14,920 --> 00:12:15,520
That doesn't make much sense.

283
00:12:16,080 --> 00:12:17,280
Basically, it just means leave.

284
00:12:17,760 --> 00:12:18,040
Okay.

285
00:12:18,080 --> 00:12:19,220
I have to leave.

286
00:12:19,460 --> 00:12:20,200
I have to get going.

287
00:12:22,400 --> 00:12:23,400
You should get going.

288
00:12:23,400 --> 00:12:24,400
You're going to be late.

289
00:12:24,400 --> 00:12:25,400
Exactly.

290
00:12:25,400 --> 00:12:26,400
Okay.

291
00:12:26,400 --> 00:12:29,320
Some really good small talk phrases that are useful in any situation.

292
00:12:29,320 --> 00:12:30,340
So why don't we hear them again?

293
00:12:30,340 --> 00:12:32,360
One more time by listening to the dialogue.

294
00:12:34,360 --> 00:12:36,680
Valerie.

295
00:12:36,680 --> 00:12:39,120
Hi.

296
00:12:39,120 --> 00:12:42,400
Wow.

297
00:12:42,400 --> 00:12:42,920
How have you been?

298
00:12:43,140 --> 00:12:44,460
It's been such a long time.

299
00:12:44,800 --> 00:12:45,180
Darlene.

300
00:12:45,760 --> 00:12:45,920
Indeed.

301
00:12:46,120 --> 00:12:46,760
It's been a while.

302
00:12:47,200 --> 00:12:47,860
How have you been?

303
00:12:48,400 --> 00:12:49,400
Wow.

304
00:12:49,400 --> 00:12:49,560
You look amazing.

305
00:12:50,400 --> 00:12:51,680
I love what you've done with your hair.

306
00:12:52,180 --> 00:12:52,560
Really?

307
00:12:53,530 --> 00:12:53,970
Thanks.

308
00:12:54,190 --> 00:12:57,430
I went to that hair salon you told me about, but enough about me.

309
00:12:57,940 --> 00:12:58,430
Look at you.

310
00:12:59,080 --> 00:13:00,080
God, you haven't aged a day.

311
00:13:00,100 --> 00:13:01,080
What is your secret?

312
00:13:01,080 --> 00:13:02,080
Come on.

313
00:13:03,470 --> 00:13:07,530
Well, I've been watching what I eat, and I work out three times a week.

314
00:13:08,290 --> 00:13:10,410
By the way, I heard your son recently graduated.

315
00:13:11,190 --> 00:13:11,530
Yes.

316
00:13:11,930 --> 00:13:14,690
My little Paul is finally a doctor.

317
00:13:15,640 --> 00:13:16,790
They grow up so fast, you know.

318
00:13:17,320 --> 00:13:18,530
He is such a handsome guy.

319
00:13:19,440 --> 00:13:20,810
He gets his looks from his mother, of course.

320
00:13:21,840 --> 00:13:22,010
Thank you.

321
00:13:23,560 --> 00:13:24,650
What about your daughter, Pamela?

322
00:13:25,360 --> 00:13:27,790
I heard she passed the bar exam and married recently.

323
00:13:28,390 --> 00:13:28,850
Oh, yes.

324
00:13:28,990 --> 00:13:32,230
She had a beautiful wedding in Cozumel, Mexico, and we all attended.

325
00:13:32,970 --> 00:13:34,570
Such a lovely girl.

326
00:13:35,290 --> 00:13:38,530
I hope my Paul is lucky enough to find a girl like that someday.

327
00:13:39,210 --> 00:13:39,630
But of course.

328
00:13:39,990 --> 00:13:42,650
Well, it's been great talking to you, but I have to get going.

329
00:13:43,110 --> 00:13:43,710
Same here.

330
00:13:44,150 --> 00:13:46,210
We'll catch up soon, maybe over coffee.

331
00:13:46,730 --> 00:13:47,590
That would be great.

332
00:13:48,090 --> 00:13:48,550
Give me a call.

333
00:13:49,120 --> 00:13:49,510
See you soon.

334
00:13:50,120 --> 00:13:51,120
Bye.

335
00:13:52,300 --> 00:13:52,940
Ugh.

336
00:13:53,220 --> 00:13:56,720
I cannot stand that woman or her obnoxious daughter.

337
00:14:04,360 --> 00:14:04,480
All right.

338
00:14:05,360 --> 00:14:06,360
Very good.

339
00:14:06,360 --> 00:14:13,240
So now you have a couple of phrases that you can use to flatter someone, be it your friend or somebody that you know or anyone.

340
00:14:13,240 --> 00:14:16,520
And well, they are very, very useful and if you use them correctly, of course.

341
00:14:16,820 --> 00:14:16,940
Right.

342
00:14:17,800 --> 00:14:20,800
And these phrases sound really honest and really natural, very native-like.

343
00:14:21,160 --> 00:14:21,340
Okay.

344
00:14:21,900 --> 00:14:32,100
So, if you have any other questions or comments or if you want to share some other phrases that you use to flatter people, come to our website at EnglishPod.com and leave them in our comment section.

345
00:14:32,800 --> 00:14:36,280
So Marco and I have to get going, but we're looking forward to seeing you on the website.

346
00:14:36,760 --> 00:14:38,640
Thanks for listening and until next time.

347
00:14:38,920 --> 00:14:39,920
Bye.

348
00:14:39,920 --> 00:14:48,320
Bye-bye.
